{# BJJ Position Template V3 - Jinja2 #}
{# Generates markdown from TEMPLATE.json data with auto-generated schema markup #}
{# A/B Testing: variant-a-show/variant-b-hide CSS classes for section testing #}

---
title: "{{ metadata.title }}"
description: "{{ metadata.description }}"
---


<!-- Schema Markup - Auto-generated from JSON -->
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Use {{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}} in BJJ",
  "description": "Complete guide to executing techniques and transitions from {{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}}.",
  "step": [
    {%- for transition in offensive_transitions[:6] %}
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "Execute {{transition.technique}}",
      "text": "From this position, execute {{transition.technique}} to transition to {{transition.target_position}}.",
      "position": {{loop.index}}
    }{{ "," if not loop.last else "" }}
    {%- endfor %}
  ],
  "tool": ["BJJ Gi or No-Gi attire", "Training partner", "Mat space"],
  "totalTime": "PT5M"
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for error in common_errors[:5] %}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens if you make this mistake: {{error.error}}?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "This leads to: {{error.consequence}}"
      }
    }{{ "," if not loop.last else "" }}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "{{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}}",
  "description": "{{metadata.description}}",
  "url": "https://bjjgraph.org/Positions/{{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip().replace(' ', '-')}}",
  "isPartOf": {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    "name": "BJJ Graph",
    "url": "https://bjjgraph.org"
  }
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Home",
      "item": "https://bjjgraph.org/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Positions",
      "item": "https://bjjgraph.org/Positions/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "{{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}}",
      "item": "https://bjjgraph.org/Positions/{{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip().replace(' ', '-')}}"
    }
  ]
}
</script>


# {{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}}
{% for tag in metadata.tags %}#{{tag}} {% endfor %}

{% if metadata.parent_variant %}
> **📌 Child Variant**: This is a **{{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}}** perspective of [[{{metadata.parent_variant}}]].
{% if metadata.sibling_variants %}
> **Sibling variants**: {% for variant in metadata.sibling_variants %}[[{{variant}}]]{{ ", " if not loop.last else "" }}{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if metadata.child_variants and not metadata.parent_variant %}
> **📋 This position has multiple perspectives**:
> {% for variant in metadata.child_variants %}[[{{variant}}]]{{ ", " if not loop.last else "" }}{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

> **Quick Answer**: {{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}} is a {{state_properties.position_type|lower}} position worth {{state_properties.point_value}} points. Advanced practitioners retain this position {{position_metrics.retention_rate.advanced}}% of the time and advance to better positions in {{position_metrics.advancement_probability.advanced}}% of exchanges.

<section id="state-properties" class="content-section">

## What Defines This Position?
- **State ID**: {{metadata.state_id}}
- **Point Value**: {{state_properties.point_value}} ({% if state_properties.point_value == 0 %}Neutral{% elif state_properties.point_value == 2 %}Advantage position{% elif state_properties.point_value == 3 %}Guard pass{% elif state_properties.point_value == 4 %}Highly dominant position{% endif %})
- **Position Type**: {{state_properties.position_type}}
- **Risk Level**: {{state_properties.risk_level}}
- **Energy Cost**: {{state_properties.energy_cost}}
- **Time Sustainability**: {{state_properties.time_sustainability}}

</section>

<section id="overview" class="content-section">

## What is {{metadata.title.split('|')[0].strip()}}?

{{overview}}

</section>

<section id="state-invariants" class="content-section">

## What Must Remain True in This Position?

{% for invariant in state_invariants -%}
- {{invariant}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="key-principles" class="content-section">

## How to Control This Position Effectively
{% for principle in key_principles -%}
- {{principle}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="prerequisites" class="content-section">

## What Do You Need Before Entering This Position?
{% for prereq in prerequisites -%}
- {{prereq}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="defensive-responses" class="content-section hide-minimal">

## How Does the Opponent Escape This Position?
{% for response in defensive_responses -%}
- [[{{response.technique}}]] → [[{{response.target_position}}]]{% if response.success_rate %} (Success Rate: {{response.success_rate}}%){% endif %}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="offensive-transitions" class="content-section">

## What Attacks Are Available From This Position?
{% for transition in offensive_transitions -%}
- [[{{transition.technique}}]] → [[{{transition.target_position}}]] (Success Rate: Beginner {{transition.success_rates.beginner}}%, Intermediate {{transition.success_rates.intermediate}}%, Advanced {{transition.success_rates.advanced}}%)
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="counter-transitions" class="content-section hide-minimal">

## How to Counter Opponent's Escape Attempts
{% for counter in counter_transitions -%}
- [[{{counter.technique}}]] → [[{{counter.target_position}}]] ({{counter.trigger}})
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="expert-insights" class="content-section expert-insight">

## What Do the Experts Say About This Position?
- **Danaher System**: {{expert_insights.danaher}}
- **Gordon Ryan**: {{expert_insights.gordon_ryan}}
- **Eddie Bravo**: {{expert_insights.eddie_bravo}}

</section>

<section id="common-errors" class="content-section hide-minimal">

## What Mistakes Do Practitioners Make in This Position?
{% for error in common_errors -%}
- {{error.error}} → {{error.consequence}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="training-drills" class="content-section hide-minimal">

## How to Train This Position
{% for drill in training_drills -%}
- **{{drill.name}}**: {{drill.description}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="related-content" class="content-section">

## Which Positions and Techniques Are Related?

{% for item in related_content -%}
- [[{{item.name}}]] - {{item.relationship}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="decision-tree" class="content-section">

## How to Make Decisions From This Position
{% for node in decision_tree -%}
{{node.condition}}:
{% for action in node.actions -%}
- Execute [[{{action.technique}}]] → [[{{action.target}}]] (Probability: {{action.probability}}%)
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="position-metrics" class="content-section">

## What Are the Success Rates for This Position?

| Skill Level  | Retention Rate | Advancement Probability | Submission Probability |
|--------------|----------------|-------------------------|------------------------|
| Beginner     | {{position_metrics.retention_rate.beginner}}% | {{position_metrics.advancement_probability.beginner}}% | {{position_metrics.submission_probability.beginner}}% |
| Intermediate | {{position_metrics.retention_rate.intermediate}}% | {{position_metrics.advancement_probability.intermediate}}% | {{position_metrics.submission_probability.intermediate}}% |
| Advanced     | {{position_metrics.retention_rate.advanced}}% | {{position_metrics.advancement_probability.advanced}}% | {{position_metrics.submission_probability.advanced}}% |

{% if position_metrics.average_time -%}
**Average Time in Position**: {{position_metrics.average_time}}
{% endif %}

</section>

<section id="optimal-submission-paths" class="content-section">

## What Are the Best Paths to Submission?
{% for path in optimal_submission_paths -%}
{{path.name}}:
{{path.path}}

{% endfor %}

</section>
